#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <string>
#include <string_view>

void write_string_prefixed_varint(hexi::binary_stream& stream, const std::string& str) {
    stream << hexi::prefixed_varint(str);
}

std::string read_string_prefixed_varint(hexi::binary_stream& stream) {
    std::string result;
    stream >> hexi::prefixed_varint(result);
    return result;
}
```

The implementation is straightforward:

1. **`write_string_prefixed_varint`**: Uses the stream's `operator<<` with `hexi::prefixed_varint(str)` to write the string with a variable-length integer prefix.

2. **`read_string_prefixed_varint`**: Creates an empty string, uses the stream's `operator>>` with `hexi::prefixed_varint(result)` to read the string, and returns the result.

The `hexi::prefixed_varint` adaptor handles the variable-length integer encoding/decoding of the string length prefix automatically, making the string representation more compact than regular prefixed strings.

